#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: decree:
#> pause: 40
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: A stately pleasure dome decree:
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: Where Alph
#> source: 2q
# 1. sed copies its input to its output, editing on the way. McMahon 1.4: 2q
# A sed program is a list of commands, [address][function][arguments], applied
# to every input line in turn. "2q" has one address (line 2) and the function q:
# quit after writing that line. Everything before it was copied unchanged.
# The data below is the paper's own sample, five lines of Coleridge; the output
# pane shows the sed command line, then this script, then the result.
# Try: change 2q to 4q, then delete the line and save: five lines come through.
2q

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
